<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/HoverCardPortal-f32f8bfd.tsx">
<change>
<description>Fix HoverCard implementation by using all required components in the correct structure</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { HoverCard, HoverCardTrigger, HoverCardContent, HoverCardPortal } from '../../../../packages/ui/components/hover-card/index';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    className: {
      type: "string",
      value: "custom-class",
      label: "Class Name",
    },
    align: {
      type: "dropdown",
      value: "center",
      options: ["start", "center", "end"],
      label: "Alignment",
    },
    sideOffset: {
      type: "number",
      value: 4,
      label: "Side Offset",
    },
  });

  return (
    <HoverCard>
      <HoverCardTrigger asChild>
        <button className="rounded-md border p-2">Hover over me</button>
      </HoverCardTrigger>
      <HoverCardPortal>
        <HoverCardContent
          className={state.className.value}
          align={state.align.value}
          sideOffset={state.sideOffset.value}
        >
          <div>Hover Card Content</div>
        </HoverCardContent>
      </HoverCardPortal>
    </HoverCard>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

The changes I made:

1. Added imports for all necessary HoverCard components (HoverCard, HoverCardTrigger, HoverCardContent)
2. Structured the component properly using all required parts:
   - HoverCard as the root component
   - HoverCardTrigger for the element that triggers the hover card
   - HoverCardPortal to portal the content
   - HoverCardContent for the actual hover card content
3. Added a trigger button to demonstrate the hover functionality
4. Applied the state properties to the HoverCardContent component where they belong

This should now work correctly as a proper HoverCard implementation. The hover card will appear when you hover over the trigger button, and the content will be properly positioned according to the alignment and offset settings.

